/-!
# The Hilbert–Serre theorem over an Artinian coefficient ring

Let `A` be a commutative ring, `σ` a finite set of `e = Fintype.card σ` variables and `M` a
finitely generated module over the polynomial ring `A[X_σ]`, integer-graded by `A`-submodules
`ℳ d` on which a homogeneous polynomial of degree `i` raises degrees by `i`. This covers every
finitely generated graded module over a standard graded `A`-algebra generated by `e` elements of
degree one, by restriction of scalars along the polynomial algebra on those generators. The
generators of `M` may have negative degrees.

Over an Artinian ring `A`, every graded piece `ℳ d` has finite length over `A`, the pieces vanish
below some degree `d₀`, and the Hilbert series `∑ₙ ℓ_A(ℳ (d₀ + n)) Tⁿ` is `h(T) / (1 - T)ᵉ` for
a polynomial `h` with integer coefficients
(`TauCeti.MvPolynomial.exists_mk_length_mul_one_sub_X_pow_eq`,
`TauCeti.GradedModule.hilbertSerre`). More generally, for any commutative ring `A` and any starting
degree `d₀ : ℤ`, the formal series of `ENat.toNat` length coefficients
`(Module.length A (ℳ (d₀ + n))).toNat` — where `ENat.toNat ⊤ = 0`, so infinite-length pieces
contribute `0` — still satisfies this rational identity
(`TauCeti.GradedModule.exists_hilbertSeries_mul_one_sub_X_pow`): a sufficiently high piece
`ℳ N₁` generates the tail `d ≥ N₁`; if some such piece `ℳ N₁` has finite length then its
annihilator quotient `A ⧸ Module.annihilator A (ℳ N₁)` is Artinian
(`TauCeti.isArtinianRing_quotient_annihilator`), reducing the tail to the Artinian case, while if
every sufficiently high piece has infinite length then all sufficiently high `ENat.toNat`
coefficients are zero. This series coincides with the genuine length Hilbert series whenever every
piece has finite length (for instance when `A` is Artinian).

Translating Mathlib's `Polynomial.hilbertPoly` by `d₀` then supplies the eventual rational Hilbert
polynomial `P : ℚ[X]` of degree strictly less than `e` agreeing with `Module.length A (ℳ d)` for
all large `d` (`TauCeti.MvPolynomial.exists_degree_lt_and_eval_eq_length`,
`TauCeti.GradedModule.hilbertSerre`). By
`TauCeti.GradedModule.exists_int_eval_of_eventually_eval_length`, any eventual polynomial for the
`ENat.toNat` length coefficients over a ring with unique additive division has degree `< e` and
takes integer values at every integer `z`. Restricting scalars along evaluation at finitely many
algebra generators that shift grading by `1` transfers the theorem to any standard finitely
generated `A`-algebra (`TauCeti.GradedModule.hilbertSerre_of_adjoin_eq_top`), and over a field
`k` lengths coincide with `Module.finrank` (`TauCeti.GradedModule.hilbertSerre_field`).

The proof inducts on the variables which do not act by zero. Multiplication by such a variable `x`
is homogeneous of degree one; its kernel `K` and cokernel `C` are graded modules on which `x` acts
by zero. In each degree `0 → K_d → M_d → M_{d+1} → C_{d+1} → 0` is exact, so additivity of length
gives `(1 - T) H_M = H_C - T H_K` for the Hilbert series. When every variable acts by zero, `M` is
finitely generated over `A`, so it has only finitely many nonzero pieces and its Hilbert series is a
polynomial.

## Main results

* `TauCeti.MvPolynomial.exists_mk_length_mul_one_sub_X_pow_eq`: below any degree under which the
  pieces vanish, the shifted Hilbert series times `(1 - T)ᵉ` is a polynomial with integer
  coefficients.
* `TauCeti.MvPolynomial.exists_degree_lt_and_eval_eq_length`: the length of the degree-`d` piece
  agrees for large `d` with a rational polynomial of degree less than `e`.
* `TauCeti.GradedModule.exists_hilbertSeries_mul_one_sub_X_pow`: rational form `h / (1 - X)ᵉ` in
  `ℤ⟦X⟧` of the shifted series of `ENat.toNat` length coefficients over any commutative ring and
  from any starting degree.
* `TauCeti.GradedModule.hilbertSerre`: the Hilbert–Serre theorem for finitely generated `ℤ`-graded
  modules over `MvPolynomial σ A` for an Artinian ring `A`.
* `TauCeti.GradedModule.exists_int_eval_of_eventually_eval_length`: degree bound and integer values
  at all integers for any eventual polynomial of the `ENat.toNat` length coefficients.
* `TauCeti.GradedModule.hilbertSerre_of_adjoin_eq_top`: the Hilbert–Serre theorem for algebras
  generated by finitely many elements that shift the module grading by `1`.
* `TauCeti.GradedModule.hilbertSerre_field`: the dimension-polynomial specialization over a field.

## References

* M. F. Atiyah and I. G. Macdonald, *Introduction to Commutative Algebra*, Addison–Wesley (1969),
  Chapter 11, Theorem 11.1 and Corollary 11.2.
* The Stacks Project, Commutative Algebra, Section 10.58, Lemmas 10.58.5–10.58.7 (tags 00K7, 00K8,
  00K9), <https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/00K9>.
-/

